[3] Candidate labelled packet theorem
  For every primitive 13-speed residual S, a source-spectrum packet P(S)
  should land in exactly one theorem bucket:
    (A) q-witness family: q_threshold(S)<=13.
    (B) AP/GW boundary atoms: q=14, strict Haar interior 0, labelled packet AP/GW.
    (C) unit-petal sporadics: C27 p=2 packet, positive open mass or rank-0 strip.
    (D) K33 sporadics: nonunit packet producing TournamentStateLift.
    (E) covering-moment family: q>14 or multiple-of-14 pressure; exact-period
        boundary maps to positive gK8/L_y moment slack.
    (F) new sporadic: any SOURCE-SPECTRUM-UNKNOWN packet.  In this audited bank,
        its count is 0.

  Computed pressure in the audited bank:
    covering-moment rows=7228
    K33/state-lift rows=3
    unit-petal rows=4
  This is a classification scaffold, not a proof of the global reduction.

