    automatic words are useful packet sidecars, but mixed fibers show they
    are not theorem-safe quotients unless exact M/q, endpoint geometry,
    and route labels remain attached.

[5] Binary fixed-margin swap-chain analogy
  Fu-Qin-Wang arXiv:2606.22636 proves an inverse-polynomial spectral
  gap for binary fixed-margin swap chains by comparing to two-row
  heat-bath moves, reducing to three rows, then splitting a scalar count
  sector from Johnson-harmonic non-scalar sectors.
  LRC14 import:
    scalar count sector       -> q_threshold, exact M, Farey excess
    three-row reduction       -> AP/GW/petal/K33 local packet atlas
    Johnson harmonic sectors  -> owner-labelled C27/K33/boundary modes
    heat-bath comparison      -> packet-preserving local replacement moves
  The proof lesson is conservative: prove comparisons only after conditioning
  on the labels that make scalar count sectors honest.

[6] Tournament Analysis
  vertices are counterexample-classification routes, not runners.
  pair observable:
    exact scale retention, boundary retention, packet-owner retention,
    state-lift visibility, covering visibility, anti-scalar guard.
  switch:
    route A -> route B iff A's retention vector is lexicographically >= B's.
  tie Hamiltonian path:
    COUNTEREXAMPLE -> Q-WITNESS -> BOUNDARY-AP-GW -> BOUNDARY-PETAL-SPORADIC -> K33-STATE-LIFT -> COVERING-MOMENT -> SHELL-ALIAS-LOOSE -> MAGNITUDE-LIAR-LOOSE -> SOURCE-SPECTRUM-UNKNOWN
